cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its corpus, please cite it."
title: "Aegis: provenance-backed, authority-aware policy verification for AI agent infrastructure actions"
abstract: >-
  Aegis verifies the operational constraints an AI agent's guardrail enforces before they drive
  a decision. Each constraint carries an integrity hash bound to a cited source and an
  authority claim naming which principal may assert that class of rule; both are checked at
  decision time, and a constraint failing either gets no vote. The repository includes a
  labelled corpus, an independent reference oracle, an adversarial suite, and a benchmark
  against OPA and LLM self-checks.
